<section class="me">
    <h2>Heeee-llo.</h2>
    <p>
      <img class="alive eerie" style="float: left" src="/images/ui/snake.png">I am Artur and I go by they/them and er/ihn. I believe that everyone needs digital real estate, and this is mine. It's a laboratory because I keep tinkering with it when I am here, and it's where lots of my thoughts are cultivated. I am an artist and researcher by day and ... by night lol.
    </p>
    </section>
    <section>

    <p>
    <h2>Weeeel-coome!</h2>
      <b>-PAST-</b><br>
      When I first went online, it was all about games. I was looking up cheats on <i>mogelpower.de</i> for Animal Crossing: Wild World, reading wild rumors about various mysteries that were all made up. I barely hold any nostalgia for Geocities, IRC and whatnot. What I did was play disturbing flash games on <i>erdbeertorte.de</i>. I loved browsing DeviantArt even though I didn't know what the hell the english meant. I played games on neopets.com even though I didn't know what the hell the english meant. I played Toontown even though I didn't know what the hell the english meant. In general, there was a huge language barrier to me which I curiously did not mind. I kept telling my friends at school to go on nick.com and not nick.de because that's where all the cool SpongeBob games were hidden away from us. Eventually I became a mod on one of the bigger German Animal Crossing communities which I to this day treasure. And while most of my time online was spent on fun games, German social media platforms turned out to be quite magical before Facebook gobbled them all up.
    </p>
    <img style="display: block; margin: 0 auto;" src="/images/ui/divider.png">
    <p>
      <b>-PRESENT-</b><br>
      I taught myself a lot of web development as a kid when I wanted to make my blogger blog all cool and hipster. I believe it's what led me to my research field. As I never really spend time on very wild and myspace-y spaces, I could never really resonate with a lot of the amazing punk and brutalist work that has been happening on Neocities. I quickly fell in love with its raw nature and yearning for <a href="https://yesterweb.org/" target="__blank">the social media periphery</a>. After all, I love finding community online, but like many other people, comfort and accessibility turned out to be crucial to how I spend my time online.
    </p>
    <img style="display: block; margin: 0 auto;" src="/images/ui/divider.png">
    <p>
      <b>FUTURE</b>
      I am dreaming of a web that strengthens community and uplifts their voices. I don't want to give in to the yearning for old times. I want the ones capable to make an effort in building bridges to spaces worth sharing. This space is for me to reflect on my time online and to brood over my online experiences. There's a lot I am struggling with when I look at central and peripheral online spaces, and I hope to make room for those doubts here.
    </p>
    <img src="/images/ui/sona-hc.png">
</section>

<section class="latest-feed">
  <h2>The Latest</h2>
  <div class="latest-grid">
    {% set latest_writing = collections.post | last %}
    {% if latest_writing %}
    <a class="latest-item" href="{{ latest_writing.url }}">
      <div class="latest-label">Writing</div>
      <div class="latest-image-wrapper">
        <img src="{{ latest_writing.data.image or '/images/ui/quaint-lab.png' }}" alt="{{ latest_writing.data.posttitle }}">
      </div>
      <div class="latest-info">
        <h3>{{ latest_writing.data.posttitle }}</h3>
        <p>{{ latest_writing.data.excerpt }}</p>
      </div>
    </a>
    {% endif %}

    {% set latest_game = collections.games | first %}
    {% if latest_game %}
    <a class="latest-item" href="{{ latest_game.url }}">
      <div class="latest-label">Game</div>
      <div class="latest-image-wrapper">
        <img src="{{ latest_game.data.image }}" alt="{{ latest_game.data.posttitle }}">
      </div>
      <div class="latest-info">
        <h3>{{ latest_game.data.posttitle }}</h3>
        <p>{{ latest_game.data.excerpt }}</p>
      </div>
    </a>
    {% endif %}

    {% set latest_artwork = collections.artwork | first %}
    {% if latest_artwork %}
    <a class="latest-item" href="{{ latest_artwork.url }}">
      <div class="latest-label">Artwork</div>
      <div class="latest-image-wrapper">
        <img src="/images/artwork/{{ latest_artwork.data.image }}" alt="{{ latest_artwork.data.posttitle }}">
      </div>
      <div class="latest-info">
        <h3>{{ latest_artwork.data.posttitle }}</h3>
        <p>{{ latest_artwork.data.comment or latest_artwork.data.description }}</p>
      </div>
    </a>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>

